<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frankfurt Parliament</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–<a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Frankfurt National Assembly</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> Parliament was the first freely elected all-German assembly, meeting in St Paul's Church in Frankfurt from May 1848 during the revolutions of that year. It drafted a liberal constitution for a united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and offered the imperial crown to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-iv-of-prussia">Frederick William IV of Prussia</a>, who refused it in 1849. The assembly then broke up.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frankfurt-parliament.jpg" alt="Frankfurt Parliament" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TRAJAN 117 This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imperial_Coat_of_arms_of_Germany_(1848).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
